<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Burhanuddin Rabbani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1940–2011</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Burhanuddin Rabbani was an Afghan Islamic scholar and leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamiat-e-islami">Jamiat-e Islami</a> party. After the mujahideen took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> in 1992 he became President of the Islamic State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, but the government was torn by civil war and lost Kabul to the Taliban in 1996. He remained the internationally recognised president until 2001 and was assassinated in 2011.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/burhanuddin-rabbani.jpg" alt="Burhanuddin Rabbani" width="320" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Combined Joint Task Force 101 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Burhanuddin_Rabbani_Cropped_DVIDS.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
